To reduce redundancy [23, 24], sequences were clustered using CD-Hit at a 90% sequence identity cutoff [25, 26]. The 10 species-specific datasets collectively comprise 12 773 ABP sequences, with per-dataset counts ranging from 249 to 3451. Each dataset was randomly partitioned into training and test sets at an 8:2 ratio, as detailed in Table 1. The distribution of \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
