The graph neural network (GGN) framework combines GNNs and GVPs. Within this framework, the GGN first performs fine-grained feature modeling. Sequence features are derived using ProtTrans, while structural features are obtained by secondary structure parameters computed from DSSP. We further incorporate multi-scale geometric features, including inter-residue \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
