\usepackage{amssymb}
\usepackage{amsbsy}
\usepackage{upgreek}
\usepackage{mathrsfs}
\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
\begin{document}
$C_\alpha - C_\beta $\end{document} vectors, radial basis function-encoded distances, positional encodings, and backbone dihedral angles. These features are partitioned into scalar and vector components and encoded as node and edge attributes in the graph, then processed jointly through GVPs. Subsequently, all node features and edge features will undergo information aggregation via the message-passing layer, yielding the processed output features. In what follows, the working principles of GNN, GVP, and the message-passing layer will be elaborated respectively.

