To further validate the practical effectiveness of GGN-ABPMIC, we performed a case study using representative sequences derived from the E. coli-related datasets reported by Szymczak et al. [41] and Li et al. [42]. Several highly similar ABP sequences were selected to assess the ability of different models to capture subtle sequence variations. As shown in Table 6, the first several sequences share typical characteristics of \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
