\usepackage{amsbsy}
\usepackage{upgreek}
\usepackage{mathrsfs}
\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
\begin{document}
$\alpha $\end{document}-helical ABPs, including similar length, high hydrophobic residue content, and conserved positively charged residues, yet their experimentally measured MIC values differ substantially. GGN-ABPMIC captures these differences more accurately, whereas AMPActiPred shows larger deviations, especially for peptides with lower MIC values.

